# Node.js

Node.js is a powerful JavaScript runtime that allows developers to run JavaScript on the server side. It is widely used for building fast, scalable web applications, APIs, and command-line tools. Unlike traditional browser-based JavaScript, Node.js can interact with files, networks, and system resources, making it ideal for backend development.

## Why Node.js is important
- It uses JavaScript, so frontend and backend developers can work in the same language.
- It is fast and efficient for handling many requests at once.
- It has a large ecosystem of packages through npm.
- It is commonly used to build modern web servers and real-time applications.

## What you will learn
- How to install and run Node.js
- How to create and execute JavaScript files
- How to use npm packages
- How to build simple server applications

## Quick Start
```bash
node --version
node app.js
```

This section is a starting point for learning backend development with Node.js.
